;; M4S pass-through chain (docs/m4s-contract.md, required fixtures):
;; (p P) --> (q (bar P)) -- an id bound from a body column flows as a VALUE
;; into a second struct construction, so q rows embed bar ids and bar rows
;; embed foo ids (nested embedding across two struct relations).  The
;; settlement obligation is the embedded-id invariant: after any flush,
;; every embedded id in a live row must decode to a live struct row --
;; asserted through the content-rendered dumps (a dangling id renders as
;; garbage, never as the constructed content; see the m5-keep fixture).
;;
;; With in = {1, 2, 3}:
;;   p = { (foo 1) (foo 2) (foo 3) }        each (input 0, nonrec 1, rec 0)
;;   q = { (bar (foo X)) : X in {1,2,3} }   each (input 0, nonrec 1, rec 0)
;; Mixed flush {-in(2), +in(4)}: p/q swap member 2 for 4; foo/bar each keep
;; 3 live ids + 1 tombstone.  A second deletion (-in(3)) leaves {1, 4} and
;; 2 live ids + 2 tombstones per struct relation.

table (in int)
struct (foo int)
struct (bar foo)
table (p foo)
table (q bar)

rule
(in X)
-->
(p (foo X))

rule
(p P)
-->
(q (bar P))
